release/

# Runtime-downloaded extensions. resolveExtensionsBase() defaults to
# `<cwd>/extensions`, so booting the engine from packages/engine drops
# downloaded extension bundles here. They are build artifacts, never sources
# (the real ones live in the zveltio-extensions repo and ship via the
# registry) — and their vendored deps otherwise fail `bun run lint`.
packages/engine/extensions/

# Local-filesystem storage driver root. STORAGE_LOCAL_DIR defaults to a
# relative path, so running the engine — or the upload tests — from
# packages/engine writes uploaded files here. Artifacts, never sources.
packages/engine/storage/

# Audit reports stay local.
#
# These enumerate unfixed findings with file:line. This repository is public,
# so committing one publishes an exploitation guide for whatever has not been
# closed yet. A `git add -A` during a release cut swept SECURITY-AUDIT.md into
# a commit once; the file was removed before it was pushed, and this makes the
# next one impossible rather than caught.
SECURITY-AUDIT*.md
AUDIT-*.md

# The vision document stays local for a different reason.
#
# It is written for whoever builds Zveltio, and it says plainly where the
# product falls short today — the dashboard that reports database tables
# instead of money, the 52 hand-written pages, the refusal message that reads
# like a doorman. That candour is what makes it useful internally and what
# makes it the wrong thing to publish: the public should see the result, not
# the path to it.
VISION.md

# Playwright — traces and reports from a local run.
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/

# DR drill reports are per-run artefacts: they carry the hostname and the
# database names of whoever ran them, and this repository is public. The drill
# writes them so an operator has something to file; git is not where they go.
docs/dr-drills/*.md

# Personal Claude Code overrides (permissions etc.) — not for the team
.claude/settings.local.json
